<Section collapsed="false" isCollapsible="true" drawButton="true" MultipleChoiceAnswerIndex="-1" MultipleChoiceRandomizeChoices="false" TrueFalseAnswerIndex="-1" EssayAnswerRows="5" EssayAnswerColumns="60"><Title><Text-field style="Heading 1" layout="Heading 1">WS1 -- Invariant reduction of a conservation law (KdV, p = 0)</Text-field></Title>
<Section collapsed="false" isCollapsible="true" drawButton="true" MultipleChoiceAnswerIndex="-1" MultipleChoiceRandomizeChoices="false" TrueFalseAnswerIndex="-1" EssayAnswerRows="5" EssayAnswerColumns="60"><Title><Text-field style="Heading 2" layout="Heading 2">Input</Text-field></Title>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L2" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">restart;
# WS1: invariant reduction of a conservation law (p = 0), Section 8.1.
# Algorithm 1 (Section 5) at p = 0: no odd variables are needed and the
# cosymmetry component psi^p is a conservation-law multiplier of F = 0.
# Example: KdV, F = u_t - u u_x - u_xxx = 0, eq. (8.1); traveling-wave
# symmetry Y = -(d_t + c d_x), characteristic phi = (u_t + c u_x)|_E;
# energy multiplier psi = u.
# Expected reduction (eq. (8.2), up to sign and an additive constant):
#   I_2 = u^3/3 + u u_xx - u_x^2/2 + c u^2/2 .
# Notation: F_form_i = F^i (called F0_form_i in Appendix B), psi_i = psi^p_i,
# phi0_i = phi^i written in internal coordinates (u_t eliminated).
# All CHECKs must print 0 (10 checkpoints).
with(DifferentialGeometry): with(JetCalculus):</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L3" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">m := 1;  K := 8;
independent_variables := [t, x];</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSJtR0YoIiIiNyNGLg==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSJLR0YoIiIpNyNGLg==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+STZpbmRlcGVuZGVudF92YXJpYWJsZXNHRig3JEkidEdGKEkieEdGKDcjRi4=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L4" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">F_form1 := u1[1] - u1[]*u1[2] - u1[2,2,2];      # u_t = u u_x + u_xxx
psi1 := u1[];                                   # energy multiplier, eq. (8.1); psi1 := 1 gives the mass CL and I_1
phi01 := u1[]*u1[2] + u1[2,2,2] + c*u1[2];      # traveling wave, on E</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SShGX2Zvcm0xR0YoLCgqJiZJI3UxR0YoRigiIiImRjE2IyIiI0YyISIiJkYxNiNGMkYyJkYxNiVGNUY1RjVGNjcjRi4=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
